<body>
<div class="stickytop">
  <header class="top">
    <button class="hbtn-ham" aria-label="Open menu">☰</button>
    <div class="brand">Waterbear Field School</div>
    <button class="cartbtn" id="cartBtn" hidden>Cart <span class="cnum" id="cartNum">0</span></button>
  </header>
    <nav class="hdrnav">
    <button class="hbtn-ham" aria-label="Open menu">☰</button>
    <a class="hbtn-mini" href="#schedule" style="background:#c8891a">Upcoming</a>
    <a class="hbtn-mini" href="#journal" style="background:#4f6675">Recent</a>
    <a class="hbtn-mini" href="#about" style="background:#1c6b4a">About</a>
  </nav>
    <nav class="menudrop" id="menuDrop">
    <a href="#schedule">Upcoming Field Days</a>
    <a href="#journal">Recent Field Days</a>
    <a href="#newsletter">Newsletter</a>
    <a href="#philosophy">Philosophy &amp; Resources</a>
    <a href="#about">About</a>
  </nav>
</div>

<div class="wrap">

  <div class="herowrap">
  {#- The hero rotator shows real sessions once any have happened, each slide
      linking to its own write-up. Until then it falls back to the topic images,
      so the top of the page is never empty on a fresh install. -#}
  {%- if collections.pastSessions.length %}
  <div class="showcase">
    {%- for s in collections.pastSessions %}
    <a class="sc-slide{% if loop.first %} on{% endif %}" href="{{ s.url }}"
       style="background-image:url({% if s.data.photos and s.data.photos.length %}{{ s.data.photoDir }}{{ s.data.photos[0] }}{% else %}{{ s.data.img }}{% endif %})">
      <span class="sc-label">{{ s.data.heading }} &middot; {{ s.data.dayShort }}</span>
    </a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  {%- else %}
  <a class="showcase" href="#about">
    <div class="sc-slide on" style="background-image:url(/v6img/pg-wood.jpg)"><span class="sc-label">Woodworking</span></div>
    <div class="sc-slide" style="background-image:url(/v6img/ws-rain.jpg)"><span class="sc-label">Working with Water</span></div>
    <div class="sc-slide" style="background-image:url(/v6img/pg-fiber.jpg)"><span class="sc-label">Fiber Arts</span></div>
    <div class="sc-slide" style="background-image:url(/v6img/pj-humanpower.jpg)"><span class="sc-label">Sculpture &amp; Fabrication</span></div>
    <div class="sc-slide" style="background-image:url(/v6img/pg-nature.jpg)"><span class="sc-label">Plants &amp; Animals</span></div>
    <div class="sc-slide" style="background-image:url(/v6img/pg-music.jpg)"><span class="sc-label">Music &amp; Instrument Making</span></div>
    <div class="sc-slide" style="background-image:url(/v6img/pg-art.jpg)"><span class="sc-label">Painting &amp; Drawing</span></div>
  </a>
  {%- endif %}

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-cta">
      <a class="hbtn hbtn-sum" href="#schedule">Upcoming Field Days</a>
      <a class="hbtn hbtn-work" href="#journal">Recent Field Days</a>
      <a class="hbtn" href="#newsletter" style="background:#8f7a00">Newsletter</a>
      <a class="hbtn" href="#about" style="background:#1c6b4a">About</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  </div>

        

  <section class="sec sec-august" id="schedule" data-name="Schedule" data-blurb="Upcoming Field Days — free, all welcome.">
    <h2 class="grp">Upcoming Field Days</h2>
    <p class="seclead"><b>All welcome.</b> Field Days run <b>10 AM to 1 PM</b>, for adults and kids 6+ (an adult caregiver needs to accompany kids under 14). Registration covers materials and keeps the day running &mdash; and if the cost would keep you away, every day has a <b>pay-what-you-can</b> registration, no questions asked.</p>
    <p class="seclead" id="leadShort" hidden>Hands-on, outdoors and screen-free &mdash; for adults and kids 6+.</p>
    
    <p class="noday" id="noDays" hidden><b>Stay tuned.</b> No Field Days on the calendar just now &mdash; new dates go up here. <a href="#newsletter">Get an email when they do &rarr;</a></p>

    <div class="daycards">
      {%- set shownMonth = "" %}
      {%- for s in sessions %}
      {%- if s.month != shownMonth %}
      <h3 class="monthhead" data-month="{{ s.month }}">{{ s.month }}</h3>
      {%- set shownMonth = s.month %}
      {%- endif %}
      <article class="daycard2" id="day-{{ s.date }}" data-month="{{ s.month }}">
        <img src="{{ s.img }}" alt="">
        <div class="dc2-main">
          <a class="dc2-date" href="{{ s.path }}">{{ s.day }} · {{ s.time }}</a>
          <h3><a href="{{ s.path }}">{{ s.title }}</a></h3>
          <div class="dc2-meta">{{ s.place }}</div>
          <p class="dc2-blurb">{{ s.cardBlurb }}</p>
          <div class="dc2-actions">
            <a class="btn-reg" href="{{ s.path }}">Register</a>
            <details class="dc2-details"><summary><span class="d-more">More details ▾</span><span class="d-less">Fewer details ▴</span></summary>
              <div class="dc2-more">
                {% for p in s.about %}<p>{{ p }}</p>{% endfor %}
                <dl class="dc2-facts">
                  <div><dt>Where</dt><dd>{{ s.location }}<br><span style="color:var(--muted)">{{ s.locationNote }}</span></dd></div>
                  <div><dt>Who</dt><dd>{{ s.forWhom }}</dd></div>
                  <div><dt>Bring</dt><dd>{{ s.bring }}</dd></div>
                  <div><dt>When</dt><dd>{{ s.day }} · {{ s.time }}</dd></div>
                </dl>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="seclead" style="margin-top:14px">Want to teach a session or host one? <a href="mailto:info@waterbearfieldschool.org?subject=Field%20Days" style="color:#9a6f14;font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline">Email us</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-journal" id="journal" data-name="Recent Field Days" data-blurb="Every Field Day we've run, written up with photos." data-accent="#4f6675" data-tint="#eef1f4" data-bd="#d6dee5">
    <h2 class="grp">Recent Field Days</h2>
    {%- if collections.pastSessions.length %}
    <div class="cards">
      {%- for s in collections.pastSessions %}
      <article class="card pastday" data-date="{{ s.data.sessionSlug | truncate(10, true, "") }}"{% if not s.data.isPast %} hidden{% endif %}>
        <img class="cardimg" src="{% if s.data.photos and s.data.photos.length %}{{ s.data.photoDir }}{{ s.data.photos[0] }}{% else %}{{ s.data.img }}{% endif %}" alt="" loading="lazy">
        <div class="body">
          <h3>{{ s.data.heading }}</h3>
          <div class="when">{{ s.data.day }}{% if s.data.place %} &middot; {{ s.data.place }}{% endif %}</div>
          <div class="desc">{{ s.data.cardText }}</div>
          <div class="foot"><a class="btn-reg" href="{{ s.url }}">Read &rarr;</a></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    {%- else %}
    <p class="noday">Write-ups go up here after each Field Day.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-sub" id="newsletter" data-name="Newsletter" data-blurb="Hear when new Field Days go up." data-accent="#3f7d54" data-tint="#eef3ee" data-bd="#dbe6de">
    <h2 class="grp">Sign up for our newsletter</h2>
    <div class="subwrap">
      <p class="seclead">New Field Days as they go up &mdash; a few weeks ahead, usually capped at ten people &mdash; plus other local events, workshops and happenings we come across.</p>
      <form class="subform" id="subForm" novalidate>
        <input id="subName" type="text" name="name" placeholder="Your name (optional)" autocomplete="name">
        <input id="subEmail" type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" autocomplete="email" required>
        <button id="subBtn" type="submit">Sign up</button>
      </form>
      <p class="submsg" id="subMsg" hidden></p>
      <p class="subfine">Unsubscribe any time &mdash; or just <a href="mailto:info@waterbearfieldschool.org?subject=Unsubscribe%20me%20from%20the%20Field%20Days%20list">email us</a> and we&rsquo;ll remove you by hand.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec sec-about" id="about" data-name="About" data-blurb="What we're about — hands-on, screen-free learning on farms near Lincoln, MA." data-accent="#1c6b4a" data-tint="#eef3ee" data-bd="#dbe6de">
    <h2 class="grp">About</h2>
    <p class="about-lead">Waterbear Field School is a hands-on, outdoors skill-share for kids and adults.</p>

    <h2 class="grp" id="what-are-field-days" style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-top:24px">What are Field Days?</h2>
    <p class="seclead"><b>Field Days</b> are hands-on, outdoors, screen-free skill-shares for adults and kids 6+, running <b>10 AM to 1 PM</b>. Every day is a different mix of skills and topics — from woodworking and fiber arts to plant walks, hikes, and farm salons. Every day has a <b>pay-what-you-can</b> registration, no questions asked — registering also reserves your materials and tells us how many to expect. See what&rsquo;s coming up on the <a href="#schedule" style="color:#9a6f14;font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline">schedule</a>. You can also read about recent Field Day and Field School projects in the <a href="#journal" style="color:#4f6675;font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline">Recent Field Days</a>, or find out more about our philosophy and approach in the <a href="#philosophy" style="color:#1c6b4a;font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline">Philosophy &amp; Resources</a> section.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      {%- for w in workshops %}
      <a class="card card-link" href="/w/{{ w.slug }}/">
        <img class="cardimg" src="{{ w.img }}" alt="">
        <div class="band" style="background:{{ w.color }}"><div class="day">{{ w.title }}</div></div>
        <div class="body"><div class="desc">{{ w.blurb }}</div><div class="cardgo">See dates &amp; register &rarr;</div></div>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
      <article class="card"><img class="cardimg" src="/v6img/ws-rain.jpg" alt=""><div class="band" style="background:#2c8299"><div class="day">Working with Water</div></div><div class="body"><div class="desc">Water filters, rain catchment, pumps: cleaning and redirecting water to make it useful at home and on the farm.</div></div></article>
      <article class="card"><img class="cardimg" src="/v6img/pg-fiber.jpg" alt=""><div class="band" style="background:#4f5aa6"><div class="day">Fiber Arts</div></div><div class="body"><div class="desc">Sewing, mending, knitting and weaving — making and repairing the things we wear.</div></div></article>
      <article class="card"><img class="cardimg" src="/v6img/pj-humanpower.jpg" alt=""><div class="band" style="background:#8a5a2f"><div class="day">Sculpture &amp; Fabrication</div></div><div class="body"><div class="desc">Wire, metal and found materials — making objects that hold their own shape.</div></div></article>
      <article class="card"><img class="cardimg" src="/v6img/pg-art.jpg" alt=""><div class="band" style="background:#9a5b7a"><div class="day">Painting &amp; Drawing</div></div><div class="body"><div class="desc">Observational drawing and painting, outdoors and from life.</div></div></article>
      <article class="card"><img class="cardimg" src="/v6img/pj-trailer.jpg" alt=""><div class="band" style="background:#c05a2a"><div class="day">Build &amp; Repair</div></div><div class="body"><div class="desc">Fixing what we already own — tools, bikes, household things — instead of replacing them.</div></div></article>
    </div>
  
    <h2 class="grp" id="philosophy" style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-top:24px">Philosophy &amp; Structure</h2>
    <p class="seclead">A few things to know before you join us for a Field Day.</p>
    <div class="policy">
      <h3>Let&rsquo;s Go Outside!</h3>
      <p>Field Days are outdoor programs, and we&rsquo;ll be outside in all but extreme conditions. We keep an eye on the forecast, choose sheltered spots when we can, and take breaks as needed — but the best thing you can do is come dressed for the weather. Layers, sturdy closed-toe shoes, rain gear, sun protection, and a water bottle go a long way. We&rsquo;ll always let you know if a day calls for anything special.</p>
      <h3>Safety</h3>
      <p>Every Field Day follows established safety procedures, and our facilitators are trained in them. We review expectations with participants at the start of each day, keep group sizes manageable, and make sure the tools and activities are appropriate for the ages taking part. Children under 14 must be accompanied by an adult caregiver, who shares responsibility for their child&rsquo;s safety and participation.</p>
      <h3>Waivers</h3>
      <p>All participants (or a parent/guardian, for minors) complete a waiver form before their first Field Day. We&rsquo;ll share the form ahead of time so you can fill it out in advance and we can get started without paperwork on the day.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="policy" style="margin-top:6px">
      <h3>Structure</h3>
      <p>Waterbear Field School operates as a recreational and enrichment program, not a licensed school or daycare. We don&rsquo;t offer &lsquo;drop off&rsquo; — children under 14 must be accompanied by an adult caregiver.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="about-foot" style="margin-top:10px">Questions? <a href="mailto:info@waterbearfieldschool.org" style="color:#1c6b4a;font-weight:700">Email us</a>.</p>
  </section>

</div>

